      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is open today, although increasing winds have now closed all chairlifts for the day. The Learners Slopes remain open until 1:00 pm. The resort reports that yesterday's fresh snowfall combined with cold conditions has produced great snow, with extensive overnight grooming. Current conditions are -1°C, with winds at 45 km/h and gusts to 80 km/h. The day started clear, with high cloud expected to build and strengthening southwest winds bringing cooler air. 2/10 lifts are open: Kindy Conveyor and Learner Conveyors are operating, while all chairlifts are closed following the 10:45 am wind update. 2/10 terrain areas are open, with Learners Slopes and Ski Touring Access available; Main Basin and the remaining listed terrain are closed. The resort's scheduled opening times were Main Basin and Valley View from 8:30 am, followed by Captains, Willows, Soho and T-Bar from 9:00 am, but wind conditions have since forced the chairlifts to close. (Issued: 10:45 am, 11 Sep) The access road is chain-free, although chains must be carried, and an active road hazard advisory remains in place. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 2 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
