      "summary": "Treble Cone is open today, with the Beginner Platter operating while strong winds have restricted the remainder of the ski area. A cold, clear night has kept the recent fresh snow in great shape, with crisp conditions expected before the sun softens the snow. Current conditions are 0°C, with winds of 29 km/h and gusts to 51 km/h. The latest update reports that severe gale-force winds have forced Saddle Basin to close for the day, while Home Basin's six-seater remains on hold. 1/3 lifts is open: the Beginner Platter is operating, Home Basin Express is on hold and Saddle Quad is closed. 3/9 terrain areas are open, consisting of the Beginner Platter, Backcountry Access and Skinning Access; Home Basin, Powder Bowl and Matukituki Basin are on hold, while Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes and Motatapu Chutes are closed. (Issued: 12:30 pm, 11 Sep) The access road is chain-free, but all vehicles must carry chains. The road is narrow in places, and a free shuttle operates from the bottom of the access road. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 1 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
